This is a short appendix to a workshop I facilitated with [@0ddhost](https://www.instagram.com/oddh0st/) on how to make websites. It's one of the most common questions I get, and one of the hardest questions to answer. Here are some of the resources that helped me in my journey.

Check in on this site in the future, I will add to it as I find more resources.

![](/images/writing/workshop/poster.webp)

## Workshop Content
For the workshop, we're using [Neocities](https://neocities.org/). It is a spiritual successor to the [Web 1.0](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_2.0#Web_1.0) platform,  [geocities](https://geocities.restorativland.org/) (which today is accessible through an archive). Alternatives to Neocities are countless; but for just one, I'd recommend [Bear Blog](https://bearblog.dev/) as an ideologically infused minimalist alternative.

